Subject: expose the toolbar icon size, and record what does not float the
 toolbar

The toolbar sits at 39 DIP and this was an attempt to find out why. It is not
the icon: the strip measures 39 whether the icon is 13, 14, 16 or Chromium's 20,
just as it is 39 whether the location bar is 24 or 30, the button height 26 or
30, or the padding 3 or 7.

So the floor is a minimum reported by one of the toolbar's other children -- the
avatar, the app menu, the extensions container -- and not by any constant this
project sets. Written down so the next attempt starts from there instead of
re-testing the four that do nothing.

The parameter stays at Chromium's 20. An earlier version of this commit
defaulted it to 16, which shrank every toolbar icon and bought nothing, since
the height did not move.

Why: "it does not go lower" is not a finding; knowing which four things are not
responsible is.
Removable when: the real floor is found and either moved or accepted.
